Yes. A failed `CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY` on a unique index leaves behind an invalid index. Queries ignore it because it may be incomplete, but it is still updated on every write. Uniqueness is enforced against other transactions from the moment the second table scan begins, so the leftover invalid index can keep rejecting duplicate writes, and violations can be reported even though the build failed. The recommended recovery is to drop the index and try again.

